# DAC filter option (patches/dac_filter/README.md): play every PCM
# session through the CS43198's non-oversampling emulation (NOS = 1)
# instead of stock's fast roll-off, low latency default.
name: dac-filter-nos
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051814
gate: build refuses unless the 2 stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`; at most one dac-filter patch per build (build.py
  --dac-filter); the finished image must pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: The DAC init at 0x0305175E writes CS43198 register 0x090000
  (PCM Filter Option) from the settings byte at 0x030232A0+0x2E3:
  0x02 when the byte is 0, else 0x42/0x82/0xC2/0x22 for 1..4
  (0x0305180E..0x03051866). No code stores the byte and no settings
  string exposes it, so units play through mode 0. This patch changes
  the mode-0 immediate at 0x03051814 (movs r1, #0x02) to 0x22,
  the mode 4 value, which stock code already writes in its own branch.
  Datasheet DS1156F2 section 7.5.2 defines the bits; the init runs once
  per playback session with the outputs muted, so no pop sequence is
  needed. Bits 1 (high-pass on) and 0 (de-emphasis off) are unchanged.
expect: 0221
replace: 2221
